From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: report the boottime of beacons and probe
 responses

The driver doesn't set boottime_ns in the rx status of a beacon or probe
response, so cfg80211 has no CLOCK_BOOTTIME timestamp for the BSS and
nl80211 leaves out NL80211_BSS_LAST_SEEN_BOOTTIME.

Android's wificond then uses the TSF as the time the BSS was last seen,
and the framework drops every scan result older than the start of the
scan. The TSF is the AP's own timer, which usually starts when the AP
does, so an AP that started after the station booted, a portable
hotspot that ran out of battery and came back for example, is missing
from every scan until the station reboots. Networks whose TSF is larger
than the station's uptime stay visible.

Set boottime_ns as ath10k does since commit e6dfbc3ba90c ("ath10k: Fix
missing frame timestamp for beacon/probe-resp").

Tested-on: WCN6855 hw2.1 PCI WLAN.HSP.1.1-03125-QCAHSPSWPL_V1_V2_SILICONZ_LITE-3.6510.41

Fixes: d5c65159f289 ("ath11k: driver for Qualcomm IEEE 802.11ax devices")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
index 61b1adcdbf..91d8f1f233 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
@@ -7711,6 +7711,10 @@ static void ath11k_mgmt_rx_event(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *skb)
 	if (ieee80211_is_beacon(hdr->frame_control))
 		ath11k_mac_handle_beacon(ar, skb);
 
+	if (ieee80211_is_beacon(hdr->frame_control) ||
+	    ieee80211_is_probe_resp(hdr->frame_control))
+		status->boottime_ns = ktime_get_boottime_ns();
+
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_MGMT,
 		   "event mgmt rx skb %p len %d ftype %02x stype %02x\n",
 		   skb, skb->len,
